WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.737 line:78%
♪

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.170 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: THANK YOU FOR

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:07.107 line:78%
JOINING ME.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.608 line:78%
I'M LAWRENCE JONES.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.409 line:78%
AND TONIGHT BLUE STATES PROBLEMS

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.144 line:78%
ARE COMING TO TEXAS.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.946 line:78%
YOU MAY HAVE HEARD THAT MY HOME

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.247 line:78%
STATE OF TEXAS JUST PICKED UP

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:16.216 line:78%
TWO CONGRESSIONAL SEATS ONE FROM

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:17.784 line:78%
CALIFORNIA AND ONE FROM TEXAS.

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:19.285 line:78%
IT'S NOT HARD TO UNDERSTAND WHY

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:21.221 line:78%
TEXAS IS A GREAT PLACE TO RAISE

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.589 line:78%
A FAMILY.

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:23.890 line:78%
IT'S CLEANER, PLUS THE SCHOOL IS

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.760 line:78%
MORE PREVALENT AND THE COST OF

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.827 line:78%
LIVING IS MUCH MORE AFFORDABLE.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.262 line:78%
AMERICANS WANT TO BE FREE.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.797 line:78%
THEY DON'T LIKE BEING RESTRICTED

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.132 line:78%
BY GOVERNMENT THAT LOCKED

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:35.101 line:78%
THREATT THEM DOWN, MASKED THEM

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:37.037 line:78%
UP AND TAXED THEM INTO OBLIVION.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:38.104 line:78%
PEOPLE FLEEING TO TEXAS FROM

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:40.774 line:78%
CITIES LIKE LOS ANGELES OR NEW

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.608 line:78%
YORK MIGHT BE SURPRISED TO FIND

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.076 line:78%
FAMILIAR PROBLEMS WAITING FOR

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:44.978 line:78%
THEM IN THE LONE STAR STATE.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.513 line:78%
I MEAN, AUSTIN.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:48.148 line:78%
THE CAPITAL CITY OF AUSTIN IS

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:50.316 line:78%
FACING A CRIME PROBLEM, A DRUG

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:51.985 line:78%
PROBLEM, AND A HOMELESS PROBLEM.

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:54.521 line:78%
BASICALLY ALL THE QUALITY OF

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.388 line:78%
LIFE ISSUES BLUE STATE

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.322 line:78%
TRANSPLANTS THOUGHT THEY WERE

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.657 line:78%
LEAVING BEHIND.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:59.225 line:78%
RESIDENTS SAY THEY HAVE NEVER

00:00:57.757 --> 00:01:02.529 line:78%
SEEN ANYTHING LIKE THIS.

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:04.297 line:78%
BUT THE CITY LEADERSHIP RUN BY

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.465 line:78%
DEMOCRATS, WELL, EXCEPT FOR THE

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.166 line:78%
LONE REPUBLICAN THERE, THEY ARE

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.868 line:78%
COMPLETELY DENYING IT.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:09.235 line:78%
SO I WENT TO AUSTIN MYSELF TO

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:13.173 line:78%
SEE IT.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:14.874 line:78%
WATCH.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.475 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU ARE DOWN HERE, YOU ARE

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.509 line:78%
READY TO PARTY.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:18.211 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S A BUSY CITY.

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:19.312 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE COME OUT TO HAVE SOME FUN.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.046 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S A GREAT TIME.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.181 line:78%
EVERYBODY IS SAFE.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:28.054 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S AMERICA.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:29.089 line:78%
IT'S MY HOME.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:31.024 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: THIS USED TO BE ONE

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:32.859 line:78%
OF THE CROWN JEWELS OF AUSTIN.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:33.226 line:78%
BUT, AS CAN YOU SEE, ANOTHER

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.727 line:78%
TENT CITY.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:36.262 line:78%
&gt;&gt; NEVER BEEN LIKE THIS BEFORE.

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:36.830 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I'M A DEMOCRAT BUT I HAVE

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.997 line:78%
LEARNED MY LESSON.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:40.033 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I'M JUST FREAKED OUT.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:42.035 line:78%
&gt;&gt; SOMETHING NEEDS TO BE DONE.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.637 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: TWO YEARS AGO, THE

00:01:42.135 --> 00:01:46.806 line:78%
CITY COUNCIL VOTED TO GET RID OF

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:48.641 line:78%
A CITY ORDINANCE THAT BANNED

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.942 line:78%
CAMPING ON PUBLIC LAND AND

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.710 line:78%
PARKS.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.478 line:78%
THE RESULT 11% INCREASE IN THE

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.613 line:78%
HOMELESS POPULATION.

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:54.581 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU HAVE PEOPLE THAT ARE

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:54.914 line:78%
ASSAULTED, PEOPLE WHO ARE

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.749 line:78%
ROBBED.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:58.852 line:78%
WE HAVE HAD HOME INVASIONS.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.721 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ONE NIGHT I WAS AT MY

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:03.056 line:78%
NEIGHBOR'S HOUSE AND WE SAW THEM

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.858 line:78%
CLEANING THEIR GUNS.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.692 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YOU FOUND NEEDLES?

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.359 line:78%
&gt;&gt; YES.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.594 line:78%
ON THE FLOOR.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.795 line:78%
I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT IT WAS.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.965 line:78%
I PICKED IT UP.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:12.432 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AUSTIN IS STARTING TO LOOK

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:13.833 line:78%
LIKE SKID ROW.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.534 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THAT IS THE LAST THING I WANT

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.002 line:78%
TO HAVE HAPPEN.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:17.837 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE GUY IS WALKING AROUND

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.171 line:78%
WITH A MACHETE THREATENING

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.973 line:78%
PEOPLE.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.174 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT STARTED WITH BOX CUTTERS

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:23.143 line:78%
AS A WEAPON.

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:25.211 line:78%
NOW WE -- SADLY WE JOKE THAT WE

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.512 line:78%
ARE THE MACHETE CAPITAL OF

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.280 line:78%
TEXAS.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:28.648 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THIS MAY THE CITY RESIDENTS

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:32.152 line:78%
GOT THEIR VOICE BACK WHEN THEY

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:33.820 line:78%
VOTED IN A LANDSLIDE VICTORY TO

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:35.021 line:78%
REINSTATE PROP B WHAT IS THE

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.355 line:78%
CITY LEADERSHIP DOING HERE IN

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:37.190 line:78%
AUSTIN?

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:38.625 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THE CITY OF AUSTIN LETS THEM

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:41.227 line:78%
DO WHATEVER THEY WANT.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:44.430 line:78%
PLEASE DO YOUR JOBS.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:47.800 line:78%
LEAVE YOUR NEEDLES SO GETS

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:52.972 line:78%
LITTLE KIDS CAN GET.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:55.241 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WE AS A PEOPLE AND CITIZENS

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:56.109 line:78%
ARE LED TO FEND FOR OURSELVES.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:57.644 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: DO YOU WANT THAT TO

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.611 line:78%
BE THE IMAGE OF AUSTIN?

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.013 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ONE OF THE REASONS I DON'T

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:01.214 line:78%
LIKE THAT IMAGE BECAUSE I DON'T

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:02.949 line:78%
THINK IT'S TRUE.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:04.951 line:78%
&gt;&gt; A GUY IS WALKING AROUND RIGHT

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.285 line:78%
OUTSIDE OF CITY HALL WITH A

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:05.952 line:78%
MACHETE.

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:06.886 line:78%
THREATENING PEOPLE.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.954 line:78%
THAT'S ILLEGAL.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:10.790 line:78%
THAT'S BREAKING THE LAW.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.858 line:78%
&gt;&gt; AND WE'RE DEALING WITH THAT

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.193 line:78%
WITH A TOUGH CHALLENGE.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:16.062 line:78%
&gt;&gt; THEY VOTED TO DEFUND THE

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:17.931 line:78%
POLICE LAST YEAR AND REALLOCATE

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:19.465 line:78%
MONEY, AND, AS SUCH, OFFICERS

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:21.968 line:78%
ARE LEAVING AT VERY HIGH RATES.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:24.370 line:78%
I THINK THE CAUSE OF OUR ILLNESS

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:25.572 line:78%
THAT IS TAKING OVER OUR CITY IS

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.207 line:78%
FAILED LEADERSHIP.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.840 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I HAVE GOT TO SAY I TALKED

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.042 line:78%
WITH THE COPS.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.877 line:78%
THEY TELL ME THAT THEY WANT TO

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:32.812 line:78%
BE ABLE TO ENFORCE THE LAWS BUT

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:33.112 line:78%
THEY HAVE BEEN TOLD TO STAND

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.847 line:78%
BACK.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:36.382 line:78%
&gt;&gt; MY POLICE CHIEF TELLS ME

00:03:34.948 --> 00:03:39.719 line:78%
THAT'S NOT TRUE.

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:41.187 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I KNOW ONE THING, CONSTANT.

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:43.323 line:78%
WE ARE GOING TO VOTE THEM OUT.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:44.524 line:78%
WE COULD EITHER ESCAPE OR RUN

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:46.326 line:78%
FROM THIS PROBLEM OR FACE IT

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.793 line:78%
STRAIGHT ON AND WE CAN MAKE A

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:49.429 line:78%
POSITIVE CHANGE.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:51.164 line:78%
&gt;&gt; DO YOU HAVE A COMMITMENT TO

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:52.799 line:78%
GO AND ENGAGE THESE MEMBERS OF

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.299 line:78%
THE PUBLIC TO COME UP WITH SOME

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.634 line:78%
SORT OF SOLUTION?

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.969 line:78%
&gt;&gt; ABSOLUTELY.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.303 line:78%
IT'S MY PRACTICE AND I HAVE BEEN

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.638 line:78%
DOING THAT.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.540 line:78%
♪

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.607 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Lawrence: DON'T WORRY, GUYS.

